  "sdo:description": "GEOMIR is the Arctic-Asian-Indo-Pacific interregional geoscientific Program aiming to improve oceanfloor&#x27;s and its relations to the continental margins knowledge and to consolidate international efforts for research ocean mineral resources within the Geosystems (coastal-ocean bed-sea water) and enable their sustainable exploitation. The overall objective of the GEOMIR is the transformative considering geomapping and mineral resources data sharing by the science-based strategy based on marine expeditions, experiments and theoretical work to provide open asses of the mineral resources (ferromanganese crusts, sulphides, phosphorites, REE, noble metals, non-conventional and others) data bases. Bioresources and minerals collection Â«Marine GeoBioBankÂ» for the worldwide sharing considered.",
